All three tests pass. The implementation is complete.

## What changed

`src/store.rs:41-68` — added `pub fn rename(dir, old_id, new_id, new_title)`.

It reads the old file (`{old_id}.note`), parses it with the same `splitn(4, SEP)` as `load_all` (so a body containing the `\n---\n` separator keeps it intact), rewrites it as `{new_id}\n---\n{new_title}\n---\n{pinned_flag}\n---\n{body}`, writes that to `{new_id}.note`, then deletes the old file.

## Verified (compiled + 3 tests, then removed)

- **Moves id + title, preserves body/tags/pinned** — a pinned note with `#a #b` tags and a body containing the `\n---\n` separator round-trips: after `rename`, `load_all` returns exactly one note with `id=new1`, `title=New Title`, same body, same tags, `pinned=true`. Old file removed, new file present.
- **Missing old id** → returns an `io::Error` of kind `NotFound`.
- **Same old/new id** → title updated, body/tags intact, no deletion of the note.

## Edge cases handled

- **old_id == new_id**: writes to the same path, skips `remove_file` (otherwise it would delete the note just written).
- **Malformed old file** (not 4 SEP-delimited parts) → `InvalidData` error, no partial new file written.
- **Body containing the `\n---\n` separator** — preserved via `splitn(4, …)`.

No test file left behind; `cargo build` is clean.


